;; Clojure's suite's world extension (round 53 (1), the user, 2026-11-17: java.xml stays out of the shipped world; its
;; XML tests take it per program): a plan of :jdk-extra alone (bin/java-project, doc/go/BUILD.md, "A JDK module as the
;; program's world extension"; no :modules: the suite's Java is its fixtures' committed forms, test/java-fixtures/forms).
;; java.xml's SAX parser (clojure.xml's SAXParserFactory, clojure.test-clojure.clojure-xml) and StAX's stream reader
;; (XMLInputFactory/createXMLStreamReader, clojure.test-clojure.reflect's invoke-checks-accessibility): the measured set
;; java-xml-classes.txt, read from jdk26u's sources at the platform's pin by read-jdk, with javac's tool world's two
;; java.xml variants (no context class loader in FactoryFinder's lookups; the JDK catalog read as a resource). No
;; :outside: the suite's world is the test build's plus these classes, a call naming a class beyond them cut (M3) as in
;; javac's tool world, whose edge (jdk/javac/edge.edn) bin/clojure-tests passes to j2g beside jdk/edge.edn (D343-1 (a)):
;; without it j2g refuses the classes naming one outside (JCS69 (b)). bin/clojure-tests reads it (--aot's program, and the eval level's extended test executable,
;; --jdk-extra-build) when a namespace of namespaces.txt runs.
{:java {:jdk-extra [{:module "java.xml"
                     :classes "java-xml-classes.txt"
                     :variants ["$arbace/overlay/jdk/javac/variants/SecuritySupport.ae"
                                "$arbace/overlay/jdk/javac/variants/JdkXmlConfig.ae"]}]}}
